  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="6.2a">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:ICn">I Cn</ref> 6.2a</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="6.2a" corresp="#wit-g-a">⁊ se ðe þæs geswican wille ⁊ clænnesse healdan, hæbbe he Godes miltse ⁊ to woruldwurðscipe si he þegenlage wyrðe.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="6.2a" corresp="#wit-a">⁊ se þe þæs geswican wille ⁊ clænnesse healden, habbe he Godes miltse ⁊ to wuruldwurðscipe sy he þegenlage wyrðe.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="6.2a" corresp="#wit-d-frags">⁊ se ðe þæs geswican wille ⁊ clænnesse healdan, hæbbe he Godes miltse ⁊ to worldwurðscipe sy he þegenlaga wyrðe.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="6.2a" corresp="#wit-q">Et qui super his abstinebit et castitatem seruabit, ad profectum sempiternum Dei misericordiam habeat et ad honorem seculi taini lege dignus sit.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="6a.2a" corresp="#wit-g-a">⁊ se ðe þæs geswican wille ⁊ clænnesse healdan, hæbbe he Godes miltse ⁊ to woruldwurðscipe si he þegenlage wyrðe.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-g-a">And he who will turn from marriage and observe celibacy shall obtain the favour of God, and as worldly honour he shall enjoy the privileges of a thegn.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Und wer hiervon abstehen und Keuschheit bewahren will, erhalte er Gottes Gnade und zum weltlichen Ehrenrang sei er Thegn-Vorrechts würdig.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And whoever will desist from this and keep chastity, let him have God's mercy, and as a worldly honour let him be entitled to a thegn's rights.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="291"><ref target="clause:VAtr_9-1">V Atr 9.1</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. V Atr. 9, 1</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:Gethyn_7">Geþyncðo 7</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="393"><ref target="clause:Northleoda_5">Norðleoda 5</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares V Atr 9.1.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
